<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="38dbd25">&lt;p&gt;
    This caoability describes our approach to Training Design. Tasks and work products required to ready the people,
    groups, or organizations for future ways of working, to analyze training needs and organizational capabilities to
    support and deliver training, to develop tailored curriculum for preparing end users and other stakeholders and
    delivering training so that the change is adopted and sustained.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    When to apply this capability
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The training practice&amp;nbsp;is a key enabler in the successful implementation of major business transformation
    engagements and programs.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Getting started
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Begin by getting familiar with the tasks, work products and guidance elements of this practice. This practice
    integrates with the other components of Business Readiness.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Common pitfalls
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Don&apos;t approach training as a cookie-cutter, one size fits all exercise.&amp;nbsp; Training involves needs analysis,
    tailoring and a flexible curriculum aligned to future ways of working and the role profiles impacted by the change
    initiative.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
